  "body": "## What changed\n\n`scripts/gate.ps1` needs PowerShell, and a Mac contributor works in bash. This adds **`scripts/gate.sh`**, a bash twin for macOS and Linux:\n\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick [base]`, `batch`, `release`, and `test <name> [crate] [--exact] [--ignored]`.\n- Same SLOW_BINARIES, crate order, clippy set, and `gate-logs/<tier>-<timestamp>/` per-step logs and summary as gate.ps1.\n- Written for bash 3.2, the version macOS ships (no associative arrays, no `mapfile`).\n- Its quick tier is coarser than gate.ps1's: it runs every suite of each crate the diff touches, rather than mapping the diff to single test fns. That runs more, never less. A change to a shared crate or the manifest widens it to batch, as in gate.ps1.\n- `.gitattributes` pins `*.sh` to LF, so the shebang survives a Windows checkout; the file is committed executable.\n\nThe README Tools and PR sections name both scripts.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `bash -n` is clean.\n- `DRY_RUN=1` plans for `batch`, `quick` and `test` (crate filter, `--exact`, the no-match error) printed the same cargo commands gate.ps1 runs.\n- It has not been run for real on a Mac. The issue reporter is the check.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #129\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
